# Cello Suite No. 1 in G major, BWV 1007: Gigue (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a cheerful English-style gigue in 6/8, two beats to the
# bar, eighths in skipping patterns with a few chords. Light and
# bouncing; the suite ends in high spirits.
#
# Time signature: 6/8, 34 bars with an eighth-note upbeat (bar 34 is
# short to match). Mutopia file bwv1007-6.mid, the seventh and last
# score: checked against bwv1007_gigue.ly. Both halves repeat (A 1-12,
# B 13-34, B entered on the upbeat at the end of bar 12); the MIDI
# plays each once, so play writes them out.
#
# Range: 11 notes below B2 (the low D and G, bars 4, 12, 34) are lifted
# an octave by the converter.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 72, 136 beats with repeats, about 1:55. Track
# times (with repeats): Pablo Casals (1938) 1:39 to 1:57 by transfer,
# about 70 to 80; Pierre Fournier (Archiv, 1960) 2:03 to 2:06, about 65.
# Confirmed from track listings. 72 is a lively gigue that still lets
# the cross-string leaps speak.
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   A  1-4    G major, the theme, half close on D (4).
#      5-8    Sequence to A (8).
#      9-12   D minor colour (F, B flat), cadence in D major (12).
#   B  13-20  D major, then to E minor, cadence (20).
#      21-24  Back to D (24).
#      25-27  G minor and C minor colour (B flat, E flat).
#      28-34  Rising sequences home to G, final cadence with fermata.
#
# Bars as performed (play), numbered along the performance:
#   A 0.83-12.83, A repeat 12.83-24.83 (score x = x+12),
#   B 24.83-46.83 (score x = x+12), B repeat 46.83-68.83 (score x = x+34).

pickup 8
tempo 72 4.

play 0.833333-12.833333 0.833333-12.833333 12.833333-34.833333 12.833333-34.833333

dyn 1 f              # A, first time
dyn 12.83 mp         # A repeat, an echo
dyn 24.83 f          # B, first time
dyn 46.83 mp         # B repeat, an echo
dyn 62 f             # score 28 on: the sequences home, full to the end

rit 1.5 0.75         # into the final G and its fermata
